{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"324bb50169fbc52275a3ed8867e142f1cd8cb381e0d66a1eab99d7a9cf19ed9a","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot finding publication","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:132","src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:700","src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py","gerrit_client.py:277","_summarize()","_translate_findings()","post_vote()","get_revision_files()","render_findings_block()","parse_anchor()","build_inline_comments()"],"problem_keywords":["advisory findings invisible","gerrit review message","review bot","finding publication","llm review vote"],"propositions":["Advisory finding text is never enumerated in Gerrit review messages; only a count of advisory findings is published on both PASS and BLOCK code paths.","The location field of each finding is discarded at adapter._translate_findings before reaching the Gerrit layer, preventing any inline anchoring.","The robot_comments parameter in gerrit_client.post_vote is never supplied by production code, so advisory findings have no path to inline comments even if locations were available.","Robot comments are disabled on this Gerrit server, making the review message body the only proven surface for finding visibility.","Advisory findings are invisible to operators deciding which criteria should be promoted from advisory to blocking status."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787544089106920001,"uuid":"8f56948a-27e1-4680-8d80-d866ab48e589"}